### 9. Protected Routes Implementation
```
Implement secure routing with these patterns:

1. AUTHENTICATION CHECKING:
   - Verify authentication state before rendering protected routes
   - Redirect to login for unauthenticated users
   - Implement role-based access control

2. TOKEN VALIDATION:
   - Validate token expiration
   - Implement token refresh mechanism
   - Handle invalid tokens gracefully

3. IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLE:

import { Navigate, Outlet } from 'react-router-dom';
import { useAuth } from '../hooks/useAuth';

function ProtectedRoute({ requiredRoles = [] }) {
  const { user, isAuthenticated, isLoading } = useAuth();
  
  // Show loading state
  if (isLoading) {
    return <div>Loading...</div>;
  }
  
  // Check authentication
  if (!isAuthenticated) {
    // Redirect to login with return URL
    return <Navigate to="/login" state={{ from: location.pathname }} replace />;
  }
  
  // Check role requirements if any
  if (requiredRoles.length > 0 && !requiredRoles.includes(user.role)) {
    // Redirect to unauthorized page
    return <Navigate to="/unauthorized" replace />;
  }
  
  // Render child routes
  return <Outlet />;
}

// Usage in router setup
<Routes>
  <Route path="/login" element={<Login />} />
  
  <Route element={<ProtectedRoute />}>
    <Route path="/dashboard" element={<Dashboard />} />
    <Route path="/profile" element={<Profile />} />
  </Route>
  
  <Route element={<ProtectedRoute requiredRoles={['admin']} />}>
    <Route path="/admin" element={<Admin />} />
  </Route>
</Routes>
```

